{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The inventory application is served on node1 over TCP port 8181.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks show an active listener on *:8181 and successful HTTP 200 health, inventory API, and application-page responses through node1's managed IP. The same service, listener, and unchanged inventory data were observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ea420209d3754b8c","cmd-fa10d41c1f3c49ff"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Mandatory access control remains enforcing while the inventory application is running.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AppArmor reported all 14 loaded profiles in enforce mode, zero complain-mode profiles, and the live inventory process confined by inventory-service (enforce). These simultaneous service and MAC checks succeeded before and after reboot, with no new post-correction or post-boot denials.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ea420209d3754b8c","cmd-fa10d41c1f3c49ff"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the application, inventory data, AppArmor profile, and systemd unit directly supported the task. The initial AppArmor rules were incomplete and caused a brief restart loop; stopping the service, inspecting its logs, correcting the profile, and restarting it were causally connected corrective actions, and no failed service remained. The reboot and temporary reboot log supported the mandatory restart protocol. Package health remained intact, and the post-executor snapshot showed no failed units or abandoned reboot log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-95f2e4d5fbcb4f1a","cmd-92b3dd487b4c4e0a","cmd-be0d068b11ba405f","cmd-501853e58af74e0a","cmd-62f04b8cc33c4c14","cmd-f13b74ca60904971","cmd-9dcd86c241a9499f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart service and data state, reboot acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, listener, inventory data, and enforcing AppArmor confinement.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-sockets observation has empty output despite the direct post-reboot command showing *:8181 listening moments earlier. Because the lifecycle socket collector also returned empty output at baseline despite known SSH listeners, its socket observation appears incomplete, but this discrepancy modestly lowers confidence.","Lifecycle snapshots do not independently capture application service or data state; restart recovery is established primarily by the executor's direct pre- and post-reboot commands."]}
